functor: 1
title: hat
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`hat` · decorate · a derived object, often an estimate.

# Form

`x.hat` on a symbol, `(a + b).hat` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `x.hat` | $x.hat$ | built and cached |
| `theta.hat` | $theta.hat$ | built and cached |
| `A.hat` | $A.hat$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A derived object, often an estimate. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A mark above or below the base. The mark follows the slant of an italic letter. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

`\hat{x}` becomes `x.hat`.

